      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "10 patients with exertional angina pectoris were examined to evaluate the hemodynamic effects of 100 mg parenteral applied Imolamin. In 4 out of 7 patients the pacing-induced angina was improved after Imolamin. No significant changes were found in heart rate, mean pulmonary artery pressure, left ventricular systolic and enddiastolic pressure. The compatibility of Imolamin was good."},
